cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AI DFIR Toolkit"
message: "If you use this toolkit or its artifact catalog in research or published work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: DePalma
    given-names: Raymond
repository-code: "https://github.com/depalmar/ai-dfir-toolkit"
abstract: >-
  Tooling and reference material for digital forensics and incident response on
  AI systems. Includes a machine-readable catalog of the endpoint artifacts left
  by AI coding agents, local LLM runtimes, agentic workflow engines, and Model
  Context Protocol components - install paths, credential storage, MCP
  configurations, listening ports, process relationships, and registry keys, each
  rated by forensic value and sourcing confidence, with collection priorities for
  incident response triage. Ships vendor-neutral Sigma detection rules, an
  osquery inventory pack, and exports in ForensicArtifacts format for Plaso, GRR,
  and Timesketch.
keywords:
  - digital forensics
  - incident response
  - DFIR
  - artificial intelligence
  - AI agents
  - Model Context Protocol
  - detection engineering
  - threat hunting
  - shadow AI
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: "2026-08-11"
